[2026-03-14T21:17:15.561Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K554xD2GgRyDGtqHCmSVRQ","type":"tool_result","content":"688-- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Cancel\" button.\n689-\n690:#### Test: Write Review button appears on completed bookings without a review\n691-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A booking with status \"completed\" exists that does not have an associated review.\n692:- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Write Review\" button that is clickable.\n693-\n694:#### Test: Write Review button does not appear on completed bookings that already have a review\n695-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A completed booking exists that already has an associated review.\n696:- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Write Review\" button. Instead, it may show \"Reviewed\" text or a checkmark indicating a review was already submitted.\n697-\n698:#### Test: Clicking Write Review button navigates to review page\n699-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A completed booking with id \"booking-456\" has no review.\n700:- **Action:** User clicks the \"Write Review\" button on that trip card.\n701:- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/trips/booking-456/review` (the Write Review page).\n702-\n703:#### Test: Write Review button does not appear on pending, confirmed, or cancelled bookings\n704-- **Initial state:** User is logged in. Bookings exist with statuses \"pending\", \"confirmed\", and \"cancelled\".\n705:- **Expected:** None of these trip cards display a \"Write Review\" button. The button only appears for \"completed\" bookings.\n706-\n707-#### Test: Trip cards are ordered by check-in date\n--\n1204-#### Test: Reviews list updates after writing a new review\n1205-- **Initial state:** User is logged in, on `/profile`, and has 2 existing reviews displayed.\n1206:- **Action:** User navigates to a completed booking, writes a new review, submits it, then navigates back to `/profile`.\n1207-- **Expected:** The \"My Reviews\" section now displays 3 reviews, including the newly written review with the correct property title, rating, and comment.\n1208-\n--\n1212-- **Expected:** The reviews are displayed in reverse chronological order (newest first): \"Cozy Cabin\" (Mar 5, 2026), \"City Apartment\" (Feb 10, 2026), \"Beach Villa\" (Jan 15, 2026).\n1213-\n1214:## Page: Write Review (`/trips/:bookingId/review`)\n1215-\n1216-<!-- Components: ReviewForm, RatingSliders, PropertyBookingContext -->\n--\n1223-- **Expected:** The page displays the property context section showing the property title \"Oceanfront Villa\", the location \"Malibu, CA\", the property's main image, check-in date \"Jan 10, 2026\", check-out date \"Jan 15, 2026\", and the number of nights (5 nights).\n1224-\n1225:#### Test: Property booking context shows guest count\n1226-- **Initial state:** User is logged in with a completed booking (booking-789) for 3 guests at \"Oceanfront Villa\".\n1227-- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n1228:- **Expected:** The property booking context section displays \"3 guests\" alongside the booking dates.\n1229-\n1230:#### Test: Property booking context shows total price paid\n1231-- **Initial state:** User is logged in with a completed booking (booking-789) with a total_price of $1,250.\n1232-- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n1233:- **Expected:** The property booking context displays the total price \"$1,250\" that was paid for the booking.\n1234-\n1235-#### Test: Redirect to login if not authenticated\n1236-- **Initial state:** No user is logged in.\n1237-- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n1238:- **Expected:** The app redirects the user to `/login`. The Write Review page is not displayed.\n1239-\n1240-#### Test: Error state when booking does not exist\n--\n1260-### Component: RatingSliders\n1261-\n1262:#### Test: All six rating sliders display with default values\n1263-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review` for a completed booking.\n1264:- **Expected:** Six rating sliders are visible with labels: \"Overall\", \"Cleanliness\", \"Accuracy\", \"Communication\", \"Location\", and \"Value\". Each slider defaults to a mid-range value (e.g., 3 out of 5) or is unset, and shows the current numeric value.\n1265-\n1266:#### Test: Adjust overall rating slider\n1267:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n1268-- **Action:** User drags the \"Overall\" slider to 5.\n1269-- **Expected:** The \"Overall\" slider displays value 5. The numeric display next to the slider updates to \"5\". Other sliders remain at their previous values.\n1270-\n1271:#### Test: Adjust cleanliness rating slider\n1272:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n1273-- **Action:** User drags the \"Cleanliness\" slider to 4.\n1274-- **Expected:** The \"Cleanliness\" slider displays value 4. The numeric display updates to \"4\".\n1275-\n1276:#### Test: Adjust accuracy rating slider\n1277:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n1278-- **Action:** User drags the \"Accuracy\" slider to 2.\n1279-- **Expected:** The \"Accuracy\" slider displays value 2. The numeric display updates to \"2\".\n1280-\n1281:#### Test: Adjust communication rating slider\n1282:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n1283-- **Action:** User drags the \"Communication\" slider to 5.\n1284-- **Expected:** The \"Communication\" slider displays value 5. The numeric display updates to \"5\".\n1285-\n1286:#### Test: Adjust location rating slider\n1287:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n1288-- **Action:** User drags the \"Location\" slider to 3.\n1289-- **Expected:** The \"Location\" slider displays value 3. The numeric display updates to \"3\".\n1290-\n1291:#### Test: Adjust value rating slider\n1292:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n1293-- **Action:** User drags the \"Value\" slider to 1.\n1294-- **Expected:** The \"Value\" slider displays value 1. The numeric display updates to \"1\".\n1295-\n1296-#### Test: Rating sliders enforce 1-5 range\n1297:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page.\n1298:- **Action:** User interacts with any rating slider.\n1299-- **Expected:** The slider only allows integer values from 1 to 5 inclusive. The slider cannot go below 1 or above 5.\n1300-\n1301-#### Test: Multiple sliders can be set independently\n1302:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n1303-- **Action:** User sets \"Overall\" to 5, \"Cleanliness\" to 4, \"Accuracy\" to 3, \"Communication\" to 5, \"Location\" to 4, \"Value\" to 2.\n1304-- **Expected:** Each slider displays its independently set value. No slider affects another slider's value.\n1305-\n1306-#### Test: Rating slider visual feedback shows filled stars or highlighted segments\n1307:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page.\n1308-- **Action:** User sets the \"Overall\" slider to 4.\n1309-- **Expected:** The slider visually indicates the selected rating (e.g., filled stars up to 4 out of 5, or a highlighted slider track up to the 4 position). The visual feedback clearly distinguishes selected vs unselected portions.\n--\n1316-\n1317-#### Test: Submit button is visible\n1318:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page.\n1319-- **Expected:** A \"Submit Review\" button is visible at the bottom of the form.\n1320-\n1321-#### Test: Type a comment in the text area\n1322:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with an empty comment text area.\n1323-- **Action:** User types \"Amazing stay! The villa was beautiful and the host was very responsive.\" in the comment text area.\n1324-- **Expected:** The text area displays the typed text \"Amazing stay! The villa was beautiful and the host was very responsive.\"\n1325-\n1326-#### Test: Submit review with all ratings and comment\n1327:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page. User has set Overall to 5, Cleanliness to 5, Accuracy to 4, Communication to 5, Location to 4, Value to 4, and typed \"Wonderful experience, would definitely come back!\" in the comment area.\n1328-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Submit Review\" button.\n1329-- **Expected:** The review is submitted successfully via `POST /api/reviews`. The app navigates back to `/trips` (My Trips page). A success notification or message such as \"Review submitted successfully\" appears.\n--\n1340-\n1341-#### Test: Submit review with ratings but no comment\n1342:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page. User has set all six rating sliders (Overall: 3, Cleanliness: 3, Accuracy: 3, Communication: 3, Location: 3, Value: 3) but left the comment text area empty.\n1343-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Submit Review\" button.\n1344-- **Expected:** The review is submitted successfully (comment is optional per the data model). The app navigates back to `/trips`.\n1345-\n1346-#### Test: Submit button is disabled when ratings are not set\n1347:- **Initial state:** User navigates to the Write Review page. No rating sliders have been adjusted from their unset/default state.\n1348-- **Expected:** The \"Submit Review\" button is disabled or grayed out, preventing submission without ratings.\n1349-\n1350-#### Test: Form validation prevents submission without all ratings\n1351:- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page. User has set Overall to 5 but left other rating sliders unset.\n1352-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Submit Review\" button.\n1353-- **Expected:** The form shows a validation error indicating all ratings are required (e.g., \"Please rate all categories\"). The review is not submitted.\n1354-\n1355:#