[2026-03-14T21:17:58.780Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Loy3NEHGw277ygsYMoBPKr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the info I need. Let me also check how login works in the app - I see the tests login with `emma@example.com` and that goes to `/`. Let me check the auth flow to understand how to log in during tests.\n\nFrom the seed data:\n- Emma Wilson: `a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333`, `emma@example.com`, guest\n- Alex Rivera: `a4444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444`, `alex@example.com`, guest\n- Booking e1111111: b1111111 property, Emma (a3333333), completed, has_review=true (review already exists)\n\n\n- Booking e4444444: b4444444 property, Alex (a4444444), completed, has_review=true\n- Booking e2222222: b2222222 property, Alex (a4444444), confirmed (not completed)\n- Booking e3333333: b3333333 property, Emma (a3333333), pending\n- Booking e5555555: b1111111 property, Alex (a4444444), cancelled\n- Booking e6666666: b5555555 property, Emma (a3333333), confirmed\n\nFor testing the write review page, I need a completed booking without a review, which I don't have in the current seed data.\n\nI'm going to split the tests into two files: one for PropertyBookingContext tests and another for RatingSliders tests. To get a completed booking without a review, I'll need to log in as a user, create a booking via API, then update its status to completed using PUT since POST only creates pending bookings.\n\nLooking at the available endpoints, PUT only supports 'confirmed' or 'cancelled' statuses, so I can't directly set a booking to 'completed' through the API. The seed data has completed bookings for Emma and Alex, but both already have reviews attached. Since the database resets between tests, I could delete the existing review from one of these bookings to make it available for testing the write review flow. I'm checking the booking data for e4444444 and noting that the test specs reference data that doesn't exist in the seed, so I'll need to map the test cases to the actual bookings available. Now I'm planning out the test files: the first will cover context display and error states like missing bookings or reviews that already exist, while the second will focus on the rating sliders and their functionality.\n\nFor the login flow, I'll follow the existing test patterns by navigating to the login page and filling in credentials. I also need to set up a beforeEach hook that clears any existing reviews so I can test the write-review flow properly. Looking at the seed data more carefully, I see e1111111 has a completed booking at the Loft with a review already attached, so I'll need to handle that cleanup.\n\nFor the booking context tests, I'm pulling the actual property details from the seed data—the Cozy Downtown Loft in New York with a 5-night stay from mid-December, 2 guests, and a total of $825—rather than relying on placeholder text from the specs.\n\nNow I'm setting up the login flow and test scenarios: logging in as Alex to verify he can't access Emma's booking, using her pending booking for the incomplete status test, and checking the review-already-exists case.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6164,"cache_read_input_tokens":52292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6164,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57b6b709-e228-49db-ae11-b6aa36b4e36c","uuid":"69e4a3ba-e379-4982-8cbe-4dd9da35d9a7"}
